decisions:
  - id: ws-relay
    decision: Use WebSocket relay with hub-and-spoke topology instead of peer-to-peer mesh
    rationale: Simpler implementation, one machine serves as hub relaying to all spokes. Avoids NAT traversal complexity of mesh topology.
  - id: pairing-auth
    decision: 6-digit pairing code + HMAC-SHA256 challenge-response for authentication
    rationale: Human-friendly pairing (easy to read aloud) with cryptographic proof to prevent replay attacks. Codes rotate every 5 minutes.
  - id: transparent-sync
    decision: Relay watches outboxes and writes to inboxes — no changes to existing MCP tools
    rationale: Existing symphony_poll, symphony_send, symphony_peek all work unchanged. Networking is a transparent sync layer on the file-based mailbox model.
